@Revel @eth1M Thanks for taking a look. A couple responses:
* Yes, I've debated cutting down to 1 page, but it felt like I either ended up with a really cramped format, or missing out on key points. I'd be really interested if there are examples of other folks with 15 YOE that are able to keep it down to 1 page.
* The date format is a personal style thing, but I've always been mildly annoyed by resumes that don't have any white space. They're often really hard to parse, and when hiring managers are going through resumes within 60-180 seconds, that extra friction can be killer. I'll experiment with a couple options though.
* Fair point on whether the summary needs to include things that are already implicit given work experience. I'll re-review those, but unless it brings it down to 1 page instead of 1.5, I'd probably keep them. 

@eth1M Do you have specific recommendation on what you would cut to make the top summary more concise?

@MikeSims Sure, no need to explain things to me, explain these in the prose to the readers of your resume.
* I get that your most recent role screwed you a bit, but it sounds like you were a TPM II and not a TPM I at your FAANG Subsidiary? Either way, if you're going to drop level descriptors from your most recent role, I would consider dropping them from all roles
* I disagree with things that say to "Keep only the last 10 years". You should *focus* on the last 10 years, but I recommend alluding to previous roles with a quick couple lines to prove your 20+ YOE

